  "problem": "What is $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-{335}^{∘})$ expressed in terms of a reference angle?",
  "worked_solution": "We wish to express $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-{335}^{∘})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{\\theta }_{R},$ where ${\\theta }_{R}$ is the reference angle corresponding to the angle $\\theta =-{335}^{∘}.$\n\nFirst, we find the corresponding coterminal angle that lies in the range $[{0}^{∘},{360}^{∘}).$ We do this by adding integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ until we get our desired angle:\n\n$$\n-{335}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={25}^{∘}\\,✓\n$$\n\nNotice that our coterminal angle is acute and lies in the first quadrant. Therefore, ${\\theta }_{R}={25}^{∘},$ and we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-{335}^{∘})=\\operatorname{tan}⁡{25}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266661/assets/360e7cef8ea04255d89a23b94b9db6993feee6f04a3123aa3515942caea6931f.png)",
